<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<gpx version="1.1" creator="Good Shit" xmlns="http://www.topografix.com/GPX/1/1"><trk><name>Knorreichenstieg Asel–Scheid — Striedereiche–Scheid north via the marked Knorreichenstieg main course [planning only — not navigation-grade]</name><desc>This roughly 10.3 km one-way Knorreichenstieg walk starts at Striedereiche near Asel. Follow marked paths along Asel bay and the slopes through Katzenberg, Lindenberg, Hünselburg wall ground and Kahle Haardt’s ancient oak woods, then Kahlehaardtweg to northern Scheid. Check return transport and parking separately. Narrow rocky slopes, roots, loose rock and boulder fields require sure-footedness. Use dry, snow-free daylight; avoid wet leaves and strong winds with falling deadwood. Stay marked, leash dogs and protect habitat. Current restrictions govern access; a closed or forbidden required leg makes the walk unavailable. Climbing and time totals are approximate estimates without a surveyed profile.

Route geometry: © OpenStreetMap contributors, Open Database License (ODbL) 1.0 — https://opendatacommons.org/licenses/odbl/1-0/. Source: https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright and https://www.openstreetmap.org/api/0.6/map?bbox=8.94,51.17,9.02,51.205. Changes: complete licensed walking ways ordered along their literal adjacent source nodes for the established Asel–Scheid course; canonical display simplified using only original source vertices. No coordinate interpolation, cross-source joins or elevations. Planning only; not navigation-grade.

